            <ArticleTitle>Fishbone-induced perforated appendicitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1136/bcr-2015-209562</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">bcr2015209562</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We review the literature and describe a case of fishbone-induced appendicitis. A 63-year-old man presented with abdominal pain. Work up including a focused history and imaging revealed fishbone-induced perforated appendicitis. The patient was managed safely and successfully with laparoscopic removal of the foreign body and appendectomy.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>2015 BMJ Publishing Group Ltd.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
